Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: expose demuxed VP8 and HEVC through the video decoder

FFmpeg decodes both formats and WineDMO already maps their compressed input
to codec IDs, but the MF/DMO registrations and the transform's accepted-type
table omit them. Use the existing generic WMV-backed decoder, as GE does for
AV1, VP9 and Theora. Register and accept the same two additional subtypes;
leave every existing input/output type and its order unchanged.

Canonicalize VP8 at the demux boundary, as already done for HEVC/VP9/AV1,
instead of letting a container-specific codec_tag bypass the advertised
MFVideoFormat_VP80 subtype.

This accepts ordinary demuxed access units. It does not add HEVC_ES fragment
assembly, P010/HDR output negotiation, hardware decoding or a new parser.
Existing MF_MT_USER_DATA extradata and FFmpeg decoding/conversion remain in
charge. Apply after the SE1 Wine series. Source-contract tested only; actual
decoding, seek/flush and A/V continuity still need a new build and runtime A/B.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_media_type.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_media_type.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_media_type.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_media_type.c
@@ -365,6 +365,7 @@ static void mf_video_format_init( const AVCodecParameters *params, MFVIDEOFORMAT *f
         if (params->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_MPEG1VIDEO) format->guidFormat = MEDIASUBTYPE_MPEG1Payload;
         else if (params->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_MPEG2VIDEO) format->guidFormat = MFVideoFormat_MPEG2;
         else if (params->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_H264) format->guidFormat.Data1 = MFVideoFormat_H264.Data1;
+        else if (params->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_VP8) format->guidFormat.Data1 = MFVideoFormat_VP80.Data1;
         else if (params->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_VP9) format->guidFormat.Data1 = MFVideoFormat_VP90.Data1;
         else if (params->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_AV1) format->guidFormat.Data1 = MFVideoFormat_AV1.Data1;
         else if (params->codec_id == AV_CODEC_ID_HEVC) format->guidFormat.Data1 = MFVideoFormat_HEVC.Data1;
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
@@ -2533,6 +2533,8 @@ static const GUID *const wmv_decoder_input_types[] =
     &MFVideoFormat_theora,
     &MFVideoFormat_AV1,
     &MFVideoFormat_VP90,
+    &MFVideoFormat_VP80,
+    &MFVideoFormat_HEVC,
 };
 static const GUID *const wmv_decoder_output_types[] =
 {
diff --git a/dlls/wmvdecod/wmvdecod.c b/dlls/wmvdecod/wmvdecod.c
--- a/dlls/wmvdecod/wmvdecod.c
+++ b/dlls/wmvdecod/wmvdecod.c
@@ -69,6 +69,8 @@ HRESULT WINAPI DllRegisterServer(void)
         {MFMediaType_Video, MFVideoFormat_theora},
         {MFMediaType_Video, MFVideoFormat_AV1},
         {MFMediaType_Video, MFVideoFormat_VP90},
+        {MFMediaType_Video, MFVideoFormat_VP80},
+        {MFMediaType_Video, MFVideoFormat_HEVC},
     };
     MFT_REGISTER_TYPE_INFO wmv_decoder_mft_outputs[] =
     {
@@ -111,6 +113,8 @@ HRESULT WINAPI DllRegisterServer(void)
         {.type = MEDIATYPE_Video, .subtype = MFVideoFormat_theora},
         {.type = MEDIATYPE_Video, .subtype = MFVideoFormat_AV1},
         {.type = MEDIATYPE_Video, .subtype = MFVideoFormat_VP90},
+        {.type = MEDIATYPE_Video, .subtype = MFVideoFormat_VP80},
+        {.type = MEDIATYPE_Video, .subtype = MFVideoFormat_HEVC},
     };
     HRESULT hr;
 
